  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Born on Andros into an established shipping family, Embiricos studied at Cambridge and completed a law degree in Athens. He joined the family business in London before opening his own shipping office in New York after the Second World War. His career followed the Greek industry’s international expansion into bulk cargo and large modern fleets.\n\nWhile building his shipping interests, Embiricos assembled a private art collection of exceptional breadth, including works by Goya, Cézanne, Kandinsky, Picasso and Van Gogh. He kept many works at his home in Lausanne and rarely lent them, making the collection both admired and elusive. Estate sales after his death in 2011 revealed the scale and quality of this parallel cultural legacy.",
    "html": "<p>Born on Andros into an established shipping family, Embiricos studied at Cambridge and completed a law degree in Athens. He joined the family business in London before opening his own shipping office in New York after the Second World War. His career followed the Greek industry’s international expansion into bulk cargo and large modern fleets.</p>\r\n<p>While building his shipping interests, Embiricos assembled a private art collection of exceptional breadth, including works by Goya, Cézanne, Kandinsky, Picasso and Van Gogh. He kept many works at his home in Lausanne and rarely lent them, making the collection both admired and elusive. Estate sales after his death in 2011 revealed the scale and quality of this parallel cultural legacy.</p>\r\n",
